CODEGEN.md §5.13, §3.5: a go types-mode emit has the name plan gen/go writes from, so its public decoder Decode<T> of record Item meets the record named DecodeItem: E8005, reported at the item named second in the plan's order (the decoders come after the types).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// An item.
record Item {
  /// Its id.
  id: Int
}

/// A record whose name is Item's decoder.
record DecodeItem {
  /// Its id.
  id: Int
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", mode: types }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  a/a.canon:4:8
  go: DecodeItem is generated for both a.DecodeItem and a.Item

